<v Ira Glass>They pull a Mariah Carey because, well, they are Mariah Carey.
<v Ira Glass>[玛丽亚·凯莉演唱的《星条旗永不落》] 自由之土上

00:43:56.870 --> 00:44:06.050
<v Ira Glass>["THE STAR-SPANGLED BANNER" BY MARIAH CAREY] O'er the land of the free
<v Ira Glass>这种情况发生得如此频繁，我想大多数美国人已经把它当作一个事实接受了。但这在其他国家根本不会发生。比如，如果你看看我出生的英国，那首国歌——

00:44:06.050 --> 00:44:19.130
<v Ira Glass>This happens so often, I think most Americans have sort of accepted it as a fact. But this sort of thing just doesn't go down like that in other countries. Like, if you take the UK, where I was born, that national anthem--
<v Ira Glass>[《天佑吾王》] 上帝保佑我们仁慈的国王

00:44:19.130 --> 00:44:24.330
<v Ira Glass>["GOD SAVE THE KING"] God save our gracious king
<v Ira Glass>我根本不知道我从哪里开始加入我自己的演绎。即兴发挥并不是英国人会对《天佑吾王》做的事情，对吧？就像你只是祝愿查尔斯国王生活幸福、胜利，然后就继续前进。但当我告诉我在《美国生活》的一些同事这件事时，他们感到不可思议。就像，肯定有其他国家在国歌结尾玩花样。伙计，这是歌的结尾。你还能干什么？

00:44:24.330 --> 00:44:52.890
<v Ira Glass>I have no earthly idea where I would even begin to put my own spin on it. The ad-libbing thing is not really something Brits do to "God Save the King," right? Like, you just kind of wish King Charles a happy, victorious life, and you keep it pushing. But when I told some of my coworkers at This American Life about this, they were incredulous. Like, surely, other countries play around with the end of their national anthems. It's the end of a song, dude. Like, what else are you going to do?
<v Ira Glass>我听了所有这些，我个人很介意。所以我决心证明他们错了。我就此采访了五位在斯坦福大学、伯克利大学、北卡罗来纳大学等地的音乐学家。他们都同意我的看法。美国歌手在国歌结尾做的事情确实在其他国家很少见。这有很多原因。比如，弗朗西斯·斯科特·基，他写了《星条旗永不落》的歌词，特意选择了一种为炫技而设计的旋律。这与其他通常是进行曲或圣歌的国歌截然不同。

00:44:52.890 --> 00:45:29.980
<v Ira Glass>I heard all that, and I took it personally. So I set out to prove them wrong. I spoke to five musicologists about this at places like Stanford, Berkeley, UNC. And they all agreed with me. What American singers do at the end of a national anthem is something you really don't see much in other countries. And there are a bunch of reasons for that. Like, for one, Francis Scott Key, who wrote the lyrics to "The Star-Spangled Banner," specifically chose a melody that's designed for showing off. This is very different from other national anthems, which are often marches or hymns.
<v Ira Glass>斯科特·基选择的曲调来自英国的一个音乐家俱乐部，基本上相当于你在才艺表演中使用那种用来展示你令人难以置信的音域和嗓音的歌曲。事实上，这就是为什么大多数人很难唱这首歌的原因。原曲有一种“你没法跟我们一起唱”的能量。

00:45:29.980 --> 00:45:47.780
<v Ira Glass>The tune Scott Key picked came from a musician's club in England and was basically the equivalent of one of those songs you use at a talent show to show your incredible range and voice. In fact, that's why the song is so hard for most of us to sing. The original tune has this kind of "you can't sing with us" energy.
<v Ira Glass>[《安那克里翁之歌》] 此外，我会像我一样指导你，将维纳斯的桃金娘与巴克斯的藤蔓缠绕在一起

00:45:47.780 --> 00:45:58.900
<v Ira Glass>["THE ANACREONTIC SONG"] And besides, I'll instruct you, like me, to entwine the myrtle of Venus with a Bacchus's vine
<v Ira Glass>其他国家不像我们这样即兴创作国歌的另一个原因是——他们没有我们那种即兴音乐的传统。比如，我们有爵士乐、布鲁斯、福音音乐、黑人音乐，其中内置了你不需要总是按照乐谱唱的规则。那里有，你知道，自由什么的，个性。艾灵顿公爵在20世纪40年代做过自己的版本。刚搬到美国的伊戈尔·斯特拉文斯基也做过一个。然而，第一个主要录制出来的歌手在体育赛事中站起来并决定他们要定制《星条旗永不落》并以自己的方式演唱是相对近期的。共识都指向1968年的一次特定表演。

00:45:58.900 --> 00:46:40.420
<v Ira Glass>The other reason other countries don't improvise the way we do on their anthem is-- they don't have our tradition of improvised music. Like, we have jazz, blues, gospel, Black music, where it's built in that you don't always do what's on the page. There's, you know, freedom or whatever, individuality. Duke Ellington did his own version in the 1940s. A newly moved to the US Igor Stravinsky did one too. And yet, the first major recorded instance a vocalist got up at a sporting event and decided they were going to customize "The Star-Spangled Banner" and sing it their own way is relatively recent. The consensus all points to one particular performance of the anthem in 1968.
<v Ira Glass>那么，女士们先生们，请注意。请起立并加入我们的国歌演唱。

00:46:40.420 --> 00:46:45.940
<v Announcer>Now, ladies and gentlemen, your attention, please. Please rise and join in the singing of our national anthem.
<v Announcer>那是世界大赛的第5场。而演唱者何塞·费利西亚诺是一位大明星。他翻唱的《点燃我》（Light My Fire）那一年发行。何塞当晚被选中演唱国歌，特别是因为他的身份，一位能提供不同东西的年轻波多黎各民谣歌手。费利西亚诺不仅改变了那首歌的一行。他的版本是对整首歌的重新构思。他几乎像是试图摆脱这首歌的宏伟，转而做相反的事情，使其变得亲密。

00:46:45.940 --> 00:47:17.780
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>It was game 5 of a World Series. And the guy who sang, Jose Feliciano, was a big star. His cover of "Light My Fire" came out that year. And Jose was chosen to do the national anthem that night specifically because of who he was, a young Puerto Rican folk singer who could offer something different. Feliciano doesn't just alter that one line of the song. His version is a whole rethinking of it. It's almost like he's trying to do away with the grandeur of the song and do the opposite, make it intimate.
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>[何塞·费利西亚诺演唱的《星条旗永不落》] 宽阔的条纹和明亮的星星

00:47:17.780 --> 00:47:24.430
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>["THE STAR-SPANGLED BANNER" BY JOSE FELICIANO] Whose broad stripes and bright stars
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>历经危险的战斗

00:47:24.430 --> 00:47:28.990
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>Through the perilous fight
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>在我们注视的壁垒之上

00:47:28.990 --> 00:47:34.710
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>O'er the ramparts we watched
<v Emmanuel Dzotsi>费利西亚诺做的录音版本非常成功。他用它作为演唱会的开场曲。一年后，吉米·亨德里克斯在伍德斯托克音乐节上走得更远。

00:47:34.710 --> 00:47:45.310
<v Ira Glass>A recording Feliciano did of his version was super successful. He opened his concerts with it. And then, a year later, Jimi Hendrix goes even further at Woodstock.
<v Ira Glass>[吉米·亨德里克斯演唱的《星条旗永不落》]

00:47:45.310 --> 00:47:55.390
<v Ira Glass>["THE STAR-SPANGLED BANNER" BY JIMI HENDRIX]
<v Ira Glass>一大批人进行着这些大动作。马文·盖伊1983年在NBA全明星赛上的版本，听起来应该附带一张免费的水床。

00:47:55.390 --> 00:48:05.250
<v Ira Glass>And a whole raft of people take these big swings. There's Marvin Gaye's 1983 version at the NBA All-Star Game, which sounds like it should come with a free waterbed.
<v Ira Glass>[马文·盖伊演唱的《星条旗永不落》] 宽阔的条纹和明亮的星星

00:48:05.250 --> 00:48:17.190
<v Ira Glass>["THE STAR-SPANGLED BANNER" BY MARVIN GAYE] Whose broad stripes and bright stars
<v Ira Glass>历经危险的战斗

00:48:17.190 --> 00:48:22.390
<v Ira Glass>Through the perilous fight
<v Ira Glass>每个人现在演唱方式的灵感，出现在1991年，惠特尼·休斯顿在超级碗上的演唱。她放慢了歌曲速度，将其从3/4拍改为4/4拍，这给了她更多空间。她基本上是直着唱的，直到结尾和最后一行。

00:48:22.390 --> 00:48:41.790
<v Ira Glass>The inspiration for how everybody sings it now, that arrives in 1991, Whitney Houston at the Super Bowl. She slows the song down, changes it from 3/4 time to 4/4 time, which gives her more space. And she sings it mostly straight, until the end and that last line.
<v Ira Glass>[惠特尼·休斯顿演唱的《星条旗永不落》] 自由之土上

00:48:41.790 --> 00:48:50.590
<v Ira Glass>["THE STAR-SPANGLED BANNER" BY WHITNEY HOUSTON] O'er the land of the free
<v Ira Glass>勇士之乡

00:48:50.590 --> 00:49:02.430
<v Ira Glass>And the home of the brave
<v Ira Glass>天哪，我怀念惠特尼·休斯顿。但没错，这就是我们如何走到今天的：一种仪式，作为一名歌手，无论你的种族、音乐流派是什么，你打卡上班，做你被雇佣的工作，把歌照原本写的那样唱完，然后在结尾留两个乐句展示真正的个性。现在，我只想给你们放最后一个版本，因为这个周末，这个国家250周年纪念日，这可能是它唯一合适的场景之一了。

00:49:02.430 --> 00:49:34.200
<v Ira Glass>God, I miss Whitney Houston. But yeah, that's how we get to today, a ritual where you, as a vocalist, no matter what your race, what your genre of music, you clock in, do the job you were hired for, sing the song through like they wrote it, and you get two phrases at the end for some real personality. Now, I just want to play you one last version because this weekend, the 250th anniversary of this country, it's probably one of the only appropriate settings for it.
<v Ira Glass>这一个是直截了当的，“巴顿将军在国旗前，这些颜色永不褪色，如果你不是第一，你就是最后，你只能从我冰冷的死尸手中夺走这首国歌”版《星条旗永不落》，这是我听过的。因为场合，我想，需要它。那是1986年自由女神像100周年诞辰。演唱者是桑迪·帕蒂。

00:49:34.200 --> 00:49:59.400
<v Ira Glass>This one is the most on the nose, "General Patton in front of the American flag, these colors don't run, if you ain't first, you're last, you can take this anthem from me out of my cold, dead fingers" rendition of "The Star-Spangled Banner" I have yet heard. Because the occasion, I guess, called for it. It was the 100th birthday of the Statue of Liberty, 1986. And the singer was Sandi Patty.
<v Ira Glass>[桑迪·帕蒂演唱的《星条旗永不落》] 我们注视着星星

00:49:59.400 --> 00:50:03.880
<v Ira Glass>["THE STAR-SPANGLED BANNER" BY SANDI PATTY] We look to the stars
<v Ira Glass>国歌通常持续两分钟左右。但桑迪，她让它持续了近六分钟。她增加了所有为这个场合写的额外歌词。而且每次你以为这首歌要结束了，还有更多。我在高中音乐理论课上学到了这个版本，因为我们的老师把它用作转调的最伟大例子。我们离碧昂丝的《Love on Top》还有六个月。但无论如何，桑迪·帕蒂，她把它唱得越来越高。

00:50:03.880 --> 00:50:36.340
<v Ira Glass>The national anthem normally runs about two minutes. But Sandi, she makes it last for almost six. She adds all these extra verses that were written for the occasion. And every time you think the song's about to end, there is more. I learnt about this version in high school in a music theory class because our teacher used it as the greatest example of key changes. We were still six months away from Beyoncé's "Love on Top." But anyways, Sandi Patty, she takes it higher and higher.
<v Ira Glass>(歌唱) 美国！

00:50:36.340 --> 00:50:40.440
<v Ira Glass>(SINGING) America!
<v Ira Glass>再次。

00:50:40.440 --> 00:50:41.080
<v Ira Glass>Again.
<v Ira Glass>(歌唱) 美国！

00:50:41.080 --> 00:50:44.720
<v Ira Glass>(SINGING) America!
<v Ira Glass>再来一次。

00:50:44.720 --> 00:50:45.540
<v Ira Glass>And again.
<v Ira Glass>(歌唱) 美国！

00:50:45.540 --> 00:50:48.880
<v Ira Glass>(SINGING) America!
<v Ira Glass>再来一次。

00:50:48.880 --> 00:50:49.740
<v Ira Glass>And again.
<v Ira Glass>(歌唱) 美国！

00:50:49.740 --> 00:50:54.080
<v Ira Glass>(SINGING) America!
<v Ira Glass>我的家！

00:50:54.080 --> 00:51:01.760
<v Ira Glass>My home!
<v Ira Glass>美国！

00:51:01.760 --> 00:51:09.200
<v Ira Glass>America!
<v Ira Glass>这完全荒谬，但又，某种程度上不可思议。

00:51:09.200 --> 00:51:13.960
<v Ira Glass>It is totally ridiculous, and yet, kind of incredible.
<v Ira Glass>伊曼纽尔·佐齐。

00:51:13.960 --> 00:52:10.690
<v Ira Glass>Emmanuel Dzotsi.
<v Ira Glass>好吧，今天的节目由伊曼纽尔·佐齐、莫莉·马塞洛和我制作。制作今天节目的人包括菲亚·本宁、达娜·奇维斯、卡西·豪利、阿德里安·莉莉、塞斯·林德、米基·米克、斯托·尼尔森、罗宾·里德、玛丽莎·罗伯逊·泰克斯特、瑞安·鲁梅里、阿丽莎·希普和克里斯托弗·斯韦塔拉。我们的执行编辑是萨拉·阿卜杜拉赫曼。我们的高级编辑是戴维·凯斯滕鲍姆。今天特别感谢肖恩·柯林斯、安妮格雷特·福斯特、斯蒂芬·辛顿、内特·斯隆、尼古拉斯·马修、马克·克拉格、杰伊·艾利森、尼尔·德拉明、赛奇·米勒、安吉丽卡·巴斯蒂安、塞拉·克兰·默多克、阿什利·C·福特、安妮·布朗、查理·拉宁、邦妮·巴斯蒂安、劳拉·安·约翰逊、斯科特·塔克、睡熊沙丘之友、密歇根公共广播电台、萨尔·卢塞罗和克洛蒂尔德·约翰逊-比尔。

00:52:10.690 --> 00:52:49.430
<v Ira Glass>Well, the program was produced today by Emmanuel Dzotsi, Molly Marcello, and me. The people who put together today's show include Phia Bennin, Dana Chivvis, Cassie Howley, Adriene Lilly, Seth Lind, Miki Meek, Stowe Nelson, Robin Reid, Marisa Robertson Textor, Ryan Rumery, Alissa Shipp, and Christopher Swetala. Our managing editor is Sarah Abdurrahman. Our senior editor is David Kestenbaum. Special thanks today to Sean Collins, Annegret Fauster, Stephen Hinton, Nate Sloan, Nicholas Mathew, Mark Clague, Jay Allison, Neil Drumming, Saige Miller, Angelica Bastien, Sierra Crane Murdoch, Ashley C. Ford, Annie Brown, Charlie Lannin, Bonnie Bastian, Laura Ann Johnson, Scott Tucker, Friends of Sleeping Bear Dunes, Michigan Public, Sal Lucero, and Clotilde Johnson-Beale.
<v Ira Glass>还要感谢今天的《美国生活》合伙人乔纳森·泰勒和贝基·利布曼。我说的这些“生活合伙人”是谁？他们是已经注册并支付了一点钱来帮助我们做一件非常基本的事情的人，那就是继续制作我们的节目。如果你支持这个目标，我希望你能考虑加入他们。加入我们吧。作为感谢，你会得到各种好处——最显著的，我想，就是节目继续存在。但我们也在尝试各种东西。我已经写了两周的每周通讯了。让我们看看能持续多久。去 thisamericanlife.org/lifepartners。那个链接也在节目说明中。

00:52:49.430 --> 00:53:24.940
<v Ira Glass>Thanks also today to This American Life Partners Jonathan Teller and Becky Liebman. Who are these Life Partners I speak of? They are people who have signed up to pay a little bit of money to help us do something very basic, which is to continue making our show. If that is a goal you support, I hope you'll consider joining them. Join us. You get all kinds of perks as a thanks-- most notably, I think, just the show continuing to exist. But also, we've been experimenting with all sorts of stuff. I've been writing a weekly newsletter for two weeks now. We'll see how long it goes. Go to thisamericanlife.org/lifepartners. That link is also in the show notes.
<v Ira Glass>《美国生活》由公共广播交换台PRX提供给公共广播电台。像往常一样，感谢我们节目的联合创始人托里·马拉蒂亚先生。最近，他了解了什么是“皮肤干灰”（ashy）。我不知道。真尴尬。他不停地走到陌生人面前问——

00:53:24.940 --> 00:53:40.820
<v Ira Glass>This American Life is delivered to public radio stations by PRX, the Public Radio Exchange. Thanks, as always, to our program's co-founder, Mr. Torey Malatia. Recently, he has learned what being ashy is. And I don't know. It's embarrassing. He keeps going up to strangers and asking--
<v Ira Glass>我能看看你的膝盖吗？

00:53:40.820 --> 00:53:42.300
<v Aviva DeKornfeld>Can I see your knees?
<v Aviva DeKornfeld>我是艾拉·格拉斯，下周回来带来更多《美国生活》的故事。

00:53:42.300 --> 00:53:47.300
<v Ira Glass>I'm Ira Glass, back next week with more stories of This American Life.
<v Ira Glass>我是 Ira Glass，下周将带来更多《美国生活》的故事。
